course: dictionary
lesson: 396
title: The Appalachian Mountains
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word Appalachian tells you what a thing belongs to or comes from. It is an adjective, so it describes a noun: the Appalachian Mountains, the Appalachian Trail, Appalachian music. It starts with a capital letter because it is a place name.
explain: «The United States has the old, worn Appalachian Mountains in the east, the flat Great Plains in the middle and the high, young Rocky Mountains in the west.» The words old and worn tell you the Appalachians are not sharp and tall like the Rockies. Weather has worn them down over millions of years, so they are low now.
explain: The sentence also gives you clues about where they are. East, middle and west are in a line, so the Appalachians are on the eastern side of the country. Appalachian can also describe people, as in an Appalachian, a person from Appalachia.
fact: Appalachian means to do with the Appalachian Mountains, a long, old mountain range in eastern North America.
fact: The Appalachian Mountains run from Canada down to Alabama in the USA.
fact: «Appalachian» also describes the region of Appalachia, its people, its music and its way of life.
fact: The Appalachian Trail is a famous long hiking path.
fact: Appalachian folk and bluegrass music often use fiddles and banjos.
exercise: «Its shape is easy to remember: old, worn Appalachians in the east, the flat Great Plains in the middle and the high, young Rockies in the west.» Which mountains are old and worn? | The Rockies | The Great Plains | The Scottish Highlands | *The Appalachians
exercise: Where in the USA are the Appalachian Mountains? | In the far south-west | In the middle | In the west | *In the east
exercise: Which instruments are often used in Appalachian music? | *Fiddles and banjos | Pianos and harps | Recorders and flutes | Drums and trumpets
test: What is the Appalachian Trail? | A type of boat | A kind of desert | *A famous long hiking path | A river in Canada
test: Why are the Appalachian Mountains low and rounded? | They sit on a flat plain | They were built very recently by volcanoes | They are made of ice | *Millions of years of weather have worn them down
exam: Which of these is an Appalachian? | A desert in Arizona | *A person from Appalachia | A tall city tower | A kind of hiking boot
